Article 12

Women and Children Victims of Acts of Violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;

the right to recovery;

the right to determine their own decisions;

the right to obtain information;

the right to confidentiality;

the right to social rehabilitation;

the right to complaint handling that is appropriate, comfortable, and according to needs;

the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;

the right to assistance; and
to receive continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

